#  Setup


## Question J5 4.1
$mc1 = new_checkbox_multiple_choice();

$mc1 -> qa (
"Which of these allow you to conclude whether or not \( F \) is irrotational? ", 
"\( \dfrac{\partial F_2}{\partial x} = \dfrac{y^2-x^2}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = \dfrac{\partial F_1}{\partial y} \)",               
);

$mc1->makeLast( "\( \dfrac{\partial F_1}{\partial x} = \dfrac{2x y}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = - \dfrac{\partial F_2}{\partial y} \)",
"\( \dfrac{\partial F_2}{\partial x} = \dfrac{y^2-x^2}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = \dfrac{\partial F_1}{\partial y} \)",
"\( \int_C F \cdot d \gamma = 2\pi \) where \( C \) is the positively oriented unit circle centered at the origin.",
"\( F(x,y) \neq \nabla f(x,y) \) for any \( C^1 \) function \( f \) on \( \mathbb{R}^2 \setminus \{ (0,0) \}. \)");

## Question J5 4.1
$mc2 = new_checkbox_multiple_choice();

$mc2 -> qa (
"Which of these allow you to conclude whether or not \( F \) is conservative?", 
"\( \int_C F \cdot d \gamma = 2\pi \) where \( C \) is the positively oriented unit circle centered at the origin.",
"\( F(x,y) \neq \nabla f(x,y) \) for any \( C^1 \) function \( f \) on \( \mathbb{R}^2 \setminus \{ (0,0) \}. \)"
);

$mc2->makeLast("\( \dfrac{\partial F_1}{\partial x} = \dfrac{2x y}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = - \dfrac{\partial F_2}{\partial y} \)",
"\( \dfrac{\partial F_2}{\partial x} = \dfrac{y^2-x^2}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = \dfrac{\partial F_1}{\partial y} \)",
"\( \int_C F \cdot d \gamma = 2\pi \) where \( C \) is the positively oriented unit circle centered at the origin.",
"\( F(x,y) \neq \nabla f(x,y) \) for any \( C^1 \) function \( f \) on \( \mathbb{R}^2 \setminus \{ (0,0) \}. \)");

## Question J5 4.1
$mc3 = new_checkbox_multiple_choice();

$mc3 -> qa (
"Which of these allow you to conclude whether or not \( F \) is path-independent?", 
"\( \int_C F \cdot d \gamma = 2\pi \) where \( C \) is the positively oriented unit circle centered at the origin.",
"\( F(x,y) \neq \nabla f(x,y) \) for any \( C^1 \) function \( f \) on \( \mathbb{R}^2 \setminus \{ (0,0) \}. \)"
);

$mc3->makeLast("\( \dfrac{\partial F_1}{\partial x} = \dfrac{2x y}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = - \dfrac{\partial F_2}{\partial y} \)",
"\( \dfrac{\partial F_2}{\partial x} = \dfrac{y^2-x^2}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = \dfrac{\partial F_1}{\partial y} \)",
"\( \int_C F \cdot d \gamma = 2\pi \) where \( C \) is the positively oriented unit circle centered at the origin.",
"\( F(x,y) \neq \nabla f(x,y) \) for any \( C^1 \) function \( f \) on \( \mathbb{R}^2 \setminus \{ (0,0) \}. \)");

## Question J5 4.2
$mc4 = new_checkbox_multiple_choice();

$mc4 -> qa (
"Which of these allow you to conclude whether or not \( G \) is irrotational? ", 
"\( \dfrac{\partial G_2}{\partial x} = \dfrac{-2xy}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = \dfrac{\partial G_1}{\partial y} \)", 
"\( G(x,y) = \nabla \ln( x^2+y^2) \)"
);

$mc4->makeLast("\( \dfrac{\partial G_1}{\partial x} = \dfrac{y^2 - x^2}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = - \dfrac{\partial G_2}{\partial y} \)",
"\( \dfrac{\partial G_2}{\partial x} = \dfrac{-2xy}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = \dfrac{\partial G_1}{\partial y} \)", 
"\( \int_C G \cdot d \gamma = 0 \) where \( C \) is \( \textit{any} \) positively oriented  circle centered at the origin.",
"\( G(x,y) = \nabla \ln( x^2+y^2) \)"
);

## Question J5 4.2
$mc5 = new_checkbox_multiple_choice();

$mc5 -> qa (
"Which of these allow you to conclude whether or not \( G \) is conservative?", 
"\( G(x,y) = \nabla \ln( x^2+y^2) \)"
);

$mc5->makeLast("\( \dfrac{\partial G_1}{\partial x} = \dfrac{y^2 - x^2}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = - \dfrac{\partial G_2}{\partial y} \)",
"\( \dfrac{\partial G_2}{\partial x} = \dfrac{-2xy}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = \dfrac{\partial G_1}{\partial y} \)", 
"\( \int_C G \cdot d \gamma = 0 \) where \( C \) is \( \textit{any} \) positively oriented  circle centered at the origin.",
"\( G(x,y) = \nabla \ln( x^2+y^2) \)"
);

## Question J5 4.2
$mc6 = new_checkbox_multiple_choice();

$mc6 -> qa (
"Which of these allow you to conclude whether or not \( G \) is path-independent?", 
"\( G(x,y) = \nabla \ln( x^2+y^2) \)"
);

$mc6->makeLast("\( \dfrac{\partial G_1}{\partial x} = \dfrac{y^2 - x^2}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = - \dfrac{\partial G_2}{\partial y} \)",
"\( \dfrac{\partial G_2}{\partial x} = \dfrac{-2xy}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = \dfrac{\partial G_1}{\partial y} \)", 
"\( \int_C G \cdot d \gamma = 0 \) where \( C \) is \( \textit{any} \) positively oriented  circle centered at the origin.",
"\( G(x,y) = \nabla \ln( x^2+y^2) \)"
);

## Question J5 4.3
$mc7 = new_checkbox_multiple_choice();
$mc7 -> qa (
"Which of these allow you to conclude whether or not \( H \) is irrotational? ", 
"\( \dfrac{\partial H_2}{\partial x} = 1 = \dfrac{\partial H_1}{\partial y} \)",
"\( H(x,y) = \nabla (xy) \)"
);

$mc7->makeLast("\( \dfrac{\partial H_1}{\partial x} = 0 =  \dfrac{\partial H_2}{\partial y} \)",
"\( \dfrac{\partial H_2}{\partial x} = 1 = \dfrac{\partial H_1}{\partial y} \)",
"\( \int_C H \cdot d \gamma = 0 \) where \( C \)  is \( \textit{any} \) positively oriented  circle centered at \( \textit{any} \) point in \( \mathbb{R}^2. \)",
"\( H(x,y) = \nabla (xy) \)"
);

## Question J5 4.3
$mc8 = new_checkbox_multiple_choice();
$mc8 -> qa (
"Which of these allow you to conclude whether or not \( H \) is conservative?", 
"\( \dfrac{\partial H_2}{\partial x} = 1 = \dfrac{\partial H_1}{\partial y} \)",
"\( H(x,y) = \nabla (xy) \)"
);

$mc8->makeLast("\( \dfrac{\partial H_1}{\partial x} = 0 =  \dfrac{\partial H_2}{\partial y} \)",
"\( \dfrac{\partial H_2}{\partial x} = 1 = \dfrac{\partial H_1}{\partial y} \)",
"\( \int_C H \cdot d \gamma = 0 \) where \( C \)  is \( \textit{any} \) positively oriented  circle centered at \( \textit{any} \) point in \( \mathbb{R}^2. \)",
"\( H(x,y) = \nabla (xy) \)"
);

## Question J5 4.3
$mc9 = new_checkbox_multiple_choice();
$mc9 -> qa (
"Which of these allow you to conclude whether or not \( H \) is path-independent?", 
"\( \dfrac{\partial H_2}{\partial x} = 1 = \dfrac{\partial H_1}{\partial y} \)",
"\( H(x,y) = \nabla (xy) \)"
);

$mc9->makeLast("\( \dfrac{\partial H_1}{\partial x} = 0 =  \dfrac{\partial H_2}{\partial y} \)",
"\( \dfrac{\partial H_2}{\partial x} = 1 = \dfrac{\partial H_1}{\partial y} \)",
"\( \int_C H \cdot d \gamma = 0 \) where \( C \)  is \( \textit{any} \) positively oriented  circle centered at \( \textit{any} \) point in \( \mathbb{R}^2. \)",
"\( H(x,y) = \nabla (xy) \)"
);


###########################
#  Main text

Context()->texStrings;
BEGIN_TEXT
1. Define \( F(x,y) = \Big( -\dfrac{y}{x^2+y^2}, \dfrac{x}{x^2+y^2} \Big) \) on \( \mathbb{R}^2 \setminus \{ (0,0) \}. \) You have done some computations. $BR
(a) \( \dfrac{\partial F_1}{\partial x} = \dfrac{2x y}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = - \dfrac{\partial F_2}{\partial y} \) $BR
(b) \( \dfrac{\partial F_2}{\partial x} = \dfrac{y^2-x^2}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = \dfrac{\partial F_1}{\partial y} \)  $BR
(c) \( \int_C F \cdot d \gamma = 2\pi \) where \( C \) is the positively oriented unit circle centered at the origin. $BR
(d) \( F(x,y) \neq \nabla f(x,y) \) for any \( C^1 \) function \( f \) on \( \mathbb{R}^2 \setminus \{ (0,0) \}. \)
$BR
$BR
\{ $mc1 -> print_q() \}
\{ $mc1 -> print_a() \}
$BR
\{ $mc2 -> print_q() \}
\{ $mc2 -> print_a() \}
$BR
\{ $mc3 -> print_q() \}
\{ $mc3 -> print_a() \}
$BR $BR

2. Define \( G(x,y) = \Big( \dfrac{x}{x^2+y^2}, \dfrac{y}{x^2+y^2} \Big) \) on \( \mathbb{R}^2 \setminus \{ (0,0) \} \). You have done some computations. $BR
(a) \( \dfrac{\partial G_1}{\partial x} = \dfrac{y^2 - x^2}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = - \dfrac{\partial G_2}{\partial y} \) $BR
(b) \( \dfrac{\partial G_2}{\partial x} = \dfrac{-2xy}{(x^2+y^2)^2} = \dfrac{\partial G_1}{\partial y} \) $BR
(c) \( \int_C G \cdot d \gamma = 0 \) where \( C \) is \( \textit{any} \) positively oriented  circle centered at the origin. $BR
(d) \( G(x,y) = \nabla \ln( x^2+y^2) \) $BR
$BR

\{ $mc4 -> print_q() \}
\{ $mc4 -> print_a() \}
$BR
\{ $mc5 -> print_q() \}
\{ $mc5 -> print_a() \}
$BR
\{ $mc6 -> print_q() \}
\{ $mc6 -> print_a() \}
$BR $BR

3. Define \( H(x,y) = (y,x) \) on \( \mathbb{R}^2. \) You have done some computations. $BR
(a) \( \dfrac{\partial H_1}{\partial x} = 0 =  \dfrac{\partial H_2}{\partial y} \) $BR
(b) \( \dfrac{\partial H_2}{\partial x} = 1 = \dfrac{\partial H_1}{\partial y} \) $BR
(c) \( \int_C H \cdot d \gamma = 0 \) where \( C \)  is \( \textit{any} \) positively oriented  circle centered at \( \textit{any} \) point in \( \mathbb{R}^2. \) $BR
(d) \( H(x,y) = \nabla (xy) \) $BR $BR
\{ $mc7 -> print_q() \}
\{ $mc7 -> print_a() \}
$BR
\{ $mc8 -> print_q() \}
\{ $mc8 -> print_a() \}
$BR
\{ $mc9 -> print_q() \}
\{ $mc9 -> print_a() \}
$BR $BR

END_TEXT
